                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1d95d559-1f29-424d-b1be-3c67c7be7fb2",
                        "source_entry_id": "b5375216-853c-3d4a-92a0-c2a0ee7e5372",
                        "source_sense_id": "2e2a8876-524b-3a1f-9fb4-52696cb62b70",
                        "target_lang_word": "histamine",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "histamine",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "15116ed5-c7b0-3266-8791-32e73c1a4123",
                                        "entry_id": "d1cde0c8-2730-3ae8-90e1-cea0322ab93d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An amine, C₅H₉N₃, formed by decarboxylation of histidine, that causes dilatation of capillaries, contraction of smooth muscle, and stimulation of gastric acid secretion; it is released during allergic reactions."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bcc78ba2-8017-4041-ae4b-2f8624e6f432",
                                                "sense_id": "15116ed5-c7b0-3266-8791-32e73c1a4123",
                                                "text": "Mellanby and Twort have isolated from the fæces a bacillus which is able to produce from one of the amino acids normally formed in digestion of proteins a highly active body, histamine."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f3a06545-f438-4fc4-9941-041f41455b4d",
                                                "sense_id": "15116ed5-c7b0-3266-8791-32e73c1a4123",
                                                "text": "The intake of food triggers a release of histamine, which activates the acid-secreting cells."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cf115f04-afa3-4166-8dda-a1d219c852e1",
                                                "sense_id": "15116ed5-c7b0-3266-8791-32e73c1a4123",
                                                "text": "In a strongly ripened cheese, the casein proteins are broken down to amino acids, and the amino acids can be broken down into amines, small molecules that can serve as chemical signals in the human body. Histamine and tyramine are found in large quantities in Cheddar, blue, Swiss, and Dutch-style cheeses, and can cause a rise in blood pressure, headaches, and rashes in people who are especially sensitive to them."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "52d2b0f6-17af-4447-8ddd-526e16d64ed9",
                        "source_entry_id": "b5375216-853c-3d4a-92a0-c2a0ee7e5372",
                        "source_sense_id": "2e2a8876-524b-3a1f-9fb4-52696cb62b70",
                        "target_lang_word": "histamine",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "histamine",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bce0f6da-2840-3719-a6b9-72c5c5bf191c",
                                        "entry_id": "49b5b13b-1340-3615-8ebb-67d79b0ea45d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Médiateur chimique synthétisé par les granulocytes éosinophiles et les mastocytes, de formule chimique brute C₅H₉N₃."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "691a6f72-6dda-473c-ae35-e94975990f29",
                                                "sense_id": "bce0f6da-2840-3719-a6b9-72c5c5bf191c",
                                                "text": "En s'intéressant aux mécanismes de l’éveil et de la vigilance, l’équipe de Jian-Sheng Lin, directeur de recherche à l’Inserm, a mis en évidence le rôle respectif de l’orexine et de l’histamine, deux neurotransmetteurs dont le déficit entraîne la somnolence."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "58789ab8-f23f-4714-be01-d56a82a17ff6",
                                                "sense_id": "bce0f6da-2840-3719-a6b9-72c5c5bf191c",
                                                "text": "En dégageant de l’histamine, ils provoquent des céphalées, voire, selon les allergologues, des rhinorrhées, des éternuements, des démangeaisons, de l’urticaire, des douleurs abdominales et même, pour les plus sensibles, de l’asthme… — (« Sulfites : Ça sulfite comme ça », Malbouffe, le dico, Les Dossiers du Canard enchaîné nᵒ 147, avril 2018, page 77)"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7ff2d259-5ea7-4a90-8cad-61965c4b435c",
                                                "sense_id": "bce0f6da-2840-3719-a6b9-72c5c5bf191c",
                                                "text": "Et les orties pareil, avec leurs dards tout gorgés d’histamine (décidément, la nature), tentons de les éviter, voilà, on y va doucement – donnez-moi la main, je vous guide."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ba73cf03-82b4-4402-aae4-552cb5ce8814",
                        "source_entry_id": "b5375216-853c-3d4a-92a0-c2a0ee7e5372",
                        "source_sense_id": "2e2a8876-524b-3a1f-9fb4-52696cb62b70",
